        "name": "sketch.ino",
        "content": "// Mode switch: a button cycles through modes shown on three LEDs.\nconst int buttonPin = 2;             // to ground: INPUT_PULLUP, LOW while pressed\nconst int ledPins[3] = {13, 9, 7};   // modes 1, 2 and 3\nconst int potPin = A0;               // sets the blink period in mode 3\n\nconst unsigned long debounceMs = 30; // a level counts once it has held this long\nconst unsigned long holdMs = 1000;   // holding the button this long returns to mode 0\n\nint mode = 0;\n\nvoid setMode(int newMode) {\n  // TODO: Switch to newMode: light its LED only, and print \"mode N\" on Serial.\n}\n\nvoid setup() {\n  // TODO: Configure the pins, start Serial at 9600 baud and print \"ready\".\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  // TODO: Debounce the button. A click (released within a second) moves to the\n  // next mode and 3 wraps to 0; a press held for a second returns to mode 0 at\n  // once, and its release does nothing more.\n  // TODO: Read \"mode N\" lines from Serial and switch to that mode.\n  // TODO: In mode 3, blink the LED with a period from the potentiometer:\n  // 100 ms at 0 to 1000 ms at 1023, read continuously. Do not call delay().\n}\n"
      }
    ]
